==============================================================================
(1) THE ROTATION THE OPERATOR FORCES
==============================================================================
  The #125 operator is   (S / Lambda) (Lbar H e_R) + h.c.
  S is a total gauge singlet and is lepton-number-blind, so it carries no charge of its
  own to rotate. Invariance under S -> e^{i th} S therefore has ONE compensator available
  in the operator: e_R -> e^{-i th} e_R.

  That is a rotation of the right-handed electron alone. Decomposed:

    field        rotates?   chemical potential deposited
    ------------------------------------------------------------
    e_R          yes        mu_R = theta_dot
    e_L          no         mu_L = 0

    vector part  mu_V = (mu_R + mu_L)/2 = theta_dot / 2
    axial  part  mu_5 = (mu_R - mu_L)/2 = theta_dot / 2

  So a right-handed-only rotation is HALF VECTOR and half axial. It is not purely chiral,
  and that matters, because DERIVATION_HUNT's requirement is explicit: the object that
  keeps 'the vacuum's neutrality preserved identically' is the AXIAL one, mu_R = +mu_5,
  mu_L = -mu_5. A vector piece charges the medium.

==============================================================================
(2) WHY ONLY THE AXIAL HALF SURVIVES
==============================================================================
  The two halves have different fates in a medium, and the difference is not a
  convenience -- it is the distinction between a gauged and an ungauged charge:

  piece          charge                 gauged?    fate in the medium
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------
  vector         electron number        YES (EM)   SCREENED -- the plasma compensates
  axial          chirality              no         SURVIVES -- nothing screens it

  A vector chemical potential for a gauged charge cannot be imposed on a neutral medium:
  neutrality fixes it, and any attempt to shift it is Debye-screened. Chirality is not a
  gauge charge, so nothing compensates it; it relaxes only through the mass term, at a
  rate set by m_e, not by the plasma frequency.

  NET: a winding portal phase deposits  mu_5 = theta_dot / 2  on the electron, and the
  vector half it also deposits is screened away. What is left is precisely the
  neutrality-preserving axial potential the residue names.

==============================================================================
(3) THE MAGNITUDE, AT THE ONE EPOCH THE CORPUS PINS theta_dot
==============================================================================
  The corpus fixes theta_dot at the sphaleron era twice, and the two agree to 2%:
    (a) directly, in the ledger:  theta_dot = 59.7 eV
        (its m_1/theta_dot = 2.25 meV / 59.7 eV = 3.77e-05, as recorded)
    (b) via the recorded ratio theta_dot/H = 2.4e+06 at T_sph = 131.7 GeV,
        g* = 106.75:  H = 2.4384e-14 GeV  ->  theta_dot = 58.52 eV
    difference 2.0%, which is the T_sph choice: (a) implies T_sph = 133.0 GeV.

    Quoting the ledger's direct value:  mu_5 = theta_dot/2 = 29.9 eV

  Recorded for comparison, NOT as a match: the junction plasma frequency at the same
  epoch is w_J ~ 5.7 keV, about 200x larger. These are different objects and the
  comparison is offered only so the scale is not mistaken.

  WHAT IS NOT ESTABLISHED: whether this mu_5 is the size #146's doping needs. The docket
  fixes the doping through N_screen = 2 N_0 and the band structure, not through a stated
  mu_5 in eV, so there is no recorded number to compare against. That comparison is owed
  and it is a real way this candidate can die.

==============================================================================
(4) THE CONDITION IT INHERITS — AND IT IS NOT A NEW ONE
==============================================================================
  A chiral chemical potential needs a Dirac cone to sit on: two opposite-chirality states
  in the same representation, so that mu_R = +mu_5 and mu_L = -mu_5 seat a particle
  pocket against a hole pocket. #146's own third pass established that at the shell
  (Lambda_shell = 5.4e17 GeV) NO species is vector-like -- every left-handed field is an
  SU(2) doublet and every right-handed one a singlet -- so 'there is no Dirac cone for
  mu_5 to sit on at all'.

  The rotation above inherits exactly that condition, for the same reason: e_L and e_R
  are only two halves of one object once the Higgs has paired them. In the unbroken phase
  the compensator e_R -> e^{-i th} e_R still exists, but what it dopes is a chiral
  singlet with no partner, not a cone.

  phase                      cone exists?    charged-lepton selection   mu_5 source
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  broken (below EW)          YES             holds (q^2 weighting)      AVAILABLE
  unbroken (at the shell)    no              fails (Y^2, no cone)       unavailable

  THE TWO LINE UP EXACTLY. The charged-lepton selection and the mu_5 source hold in the
  same phase and fail in the same phase, for the same structural reason -- the pairing of
  opposite chiralities into one Dirac object.

==============================================================================
VERDICT — THE RESIDUE IS NOT AN INDEPENDENT UNKNOWN
==============================================================================
  #146 was carrying two open items that looked separate: (a) does the charged-lepton
  selection survive the shell's phase, and (b) what puts mu_5 there. They are one item.

  The source for mu_5 exists and is built from objects the corpus already owns -- #125's
  operator and baryogenesis's own mu = theta_dot -- with no new field, no new coupling
  and no new assumption. It is species-selective because the operator names the electron,
  and chiral because only e_R can absorb the phase. Its vector half is screened by the
  same neutrality the residue's own statement demands.

  And it is conditional on the broken phase, which is the condition the selection already
  carries. So #146's open count drops from two to one, and the survivor is the fork
  already registered as sec.6f's third horn: does the medium screen in the broken phase?

  STILL OWED, and both are attackable:
    * the size comparison -- mu_5 ~ 29 eV at T_sph against whatever doping the band
      structure needs, a number the docket has not stated in those units;
    * theta_dot at the epoch that actually matters. The 2.4e6 ratio is pinned at T_sph;
      if the doping is needed elsewhere, theta_dot ~ T^3 must be carried there and the
      turn budget says the winding is laid down early and saturates.
